    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_4_e1",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_10",
      "quote": "The primary objectives of this study were to (i) estimate the pooled effect of oral probiotic supplementation on clinically assessed acne severity, (ii) quantify between-study heterogeneity and explore potential sources of variability, and (iii) appraise the overall certainty and real-world applicability of the current evidence base.",
      "reason": "The manuscript explicitly states the primary objectives of the study in the introduction section."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_4_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_10",
      "quote": "we conducted an updated systematic review and meta-analysis focusing exclusively on double-blind randomized controlled trials of oral probiotics for acne vulgaris. The primary objectives of this study were to (i) estimate the pooled effect of oral probiotic supplementation on clinically assessed acne severity",
      "reason": "The review is an intervention study (oral probiotics for acne vulgaris). The text defines the population (acne vulgaris), intervention (oral probiotics), and outcome (clinically assessed acne severity), which constitutes a PICO-like structure for the planned comparison."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 100
}

{
  "item_id": "PRISMA_2020_5",
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e1",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_12",
      "quote": "Studies were selected according to pre-specified inclusion and exclusion criteria structured around the PICOS framework: Population: Humans diagnosed with acne vulgaris (any severity), confirmed by clinical criteria. Intervention: Oral probiotics, any strain(s), formulation, or dose. Comparator: Placebo or standard acne therapy (e.g., topical treatments). Outcomes: Quantitative acne severity outcomes (e.g., inflammatory lesion count, noninflammatory lesions, total lesion count, global acne scales). Study Design: Double-blind randomized controlled trials (RCTs) lasting ≥ 4 weeks.",
      "reason": "The manuscript explicitly defines the inclusion criteria using the PICOS framework, covering population, intervention, comparator, outcomes, and study design (including duration)."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_12",
      "quote": "Exclusion criteria: ... non-non-peerreviewed abstracts.",
      "reason": "The manuscript specifies exclusion criteria regarding publication status (non-peer-reviewed abstracts). While dissemination year and language are not explicitly mentioned as exclusion criteria, the requirement is met by the specification of publication status."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e3",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_12",
      "quote": "Exclusion criteria: ... lack of extractable numeric outcomes",
      "reason": "The manuscript distinguishes between exclusion due to the nature of the study (e.g., non-RCTs) and exclusion due to the reporting of results (lack of extractable numeric outcomes)."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e4",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "The manuscript does not explicitly describe how studies were grouped for the syntheses (e.g., by intervention type, outcome measure, or population subgroup). It mentions that meta-regression and formal subgroup analyses could not be conducted, but does not define the grouping strategy used for the primary synthesis."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e5",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "There are no notable restrictions on study eligibility that require a specific rationale beyond standard systematic review methodology."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 95
}

